# Working documents (project plan / briefs), not site content
Tech4TIME-Static-Website-Plan_v3.md

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Python (tools/)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Screenshots. tools/shoot_pages.py is the FRONTEND's tool and does not exist
# in this repository — this rule arrived with the split and describes a script
# that is not here. Kept because tools/preview.py writes here too, and an
# accidental commit of a directory of PNGs is worth one line to prevent.
tools/shots/

# Runtime artefacts from the job post editor. careers.json itself IS tracked
# (it seeds a fresh deploy); its backup and the test harness router are not.
# ONE PATTERN, NOT ONE LINE PER DOCUMENT. This was ten enumerated names and it
# had already fallen behind twice — chrome.json.bak was never added when that
# screen shipped, and settings.json.bak would have been the second miss. The
# documents are listed in CONTRACT_DOCUMENTS and nowhere else needs a copy.
content/*.json.bak
content/*.tmp
.test-router-*.php

# The private store: the master key, the password hashes, the authenticator
# secrets, sessions, the attempt counters and the audit log.
#
# lib/private.php puts this BESIDE the document root — on the host at
# /home/USER/t4t-private-admin, locally at ../t4t-private-admin — so it is
# normally outside
# this repository altogether, and it refuses to run from anywhere inside the
# document root. These lines are the backstop for a stray copy: nothing here
# should ever reach a commit, and a leaked master key means every stored
# password can be attacked offline.
t4t-private/
t4t-private-admin/
.dev-private/
*.key
setup-token.txt
# The password hashes, by name as well as by directory. CLAUDE.md rule 5 names
# it, tools/build_deploy_set.py denies it and tools/check_secrets.py asserts it
# -- and it was in no .gitignore in either half, so a stray copy anywhere
# outside the private store had nothing standing between it and a commit. Both
# repositories carry this line now.
admins.json

# The upload set, assembled by tools/build_deploy_set.py on demand.
_deploy/
